second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is the genre of \\\"Collision Course\\\"?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 260, \"text\": \"Collision Course (1989 film) Collision Course is a 1989 action-comedy film starring Jay Leno as a Detroit police officer and Pat Morita as a Japanese officer forced to work together to recover a Japanese turbocharger stolen by a thief played by Chris Sarandon.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d00\", \"start\": 261, \"end\": 319, \"text\": \"It was directed by Lewis Teague and unreleased in the U.S.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d00\", \"start\": 320, \"end\": 362, \"text\": \"until 1992, when it debuted on home video.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d00\", \"start\": 363, \"end\": 562, \"text\": \"(When Morita guest-starred on \\\"The Tonight Show\\\" in 1989, with Leno serving as guest host, they recalled that the movie had run out of money on the last day of filming, with key scenes yet to be shot\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 231, \"text\": \"Collision Course (Silverberg novel) Collision Course is a science fiction novel by American author Robert Silverberg, first published in hardcover in 1961 by Avalon Books and reprinted in paperback as an Ace Double later that year.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d01\", \"start\": 232, \"end\": 323, \"text\": \"Ace reissued it as a stand-alone volume in 1977 and 1982; a Tor paperback appeared in 1988.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d01\", \"start\": 324, \"end\": 415, \"text\": \"An Italian translation was also published in 1961, and a German translation later appeared.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d01\", \"start\": 416, \"end\": 502, \"text\": \"Silverberg planned the novel as a serial for \\\"Astounding Science Fiction\\\", but John W.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d01\", \"start\": 503, \"end\": 627, \"text\": \"Campbell rejected the work and Silverberg eventually sold a shorter version to \\\"Amazing Stories\\\", where it appeared in 1959.\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 31, \"text\": \"Irwin should only play himself.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d02\", \"start\": 32, \"end\": 189, \"text\": \"It was Stainton's idea to film Steve and Terri doing a traditional nature documentary in the Australian Outback and film these scenes in a 1:85 screen ratio.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d02\", \"start\": 190, \"end\": 565, \"text\": \"In fact, nothing for the \\\"documentary\\\" scenes were ever scripted, and when the actors (from the scripted dramatic scenes that use a 2:40 screen ratio) entered the Irwins' world for a few brief scenes, Steve (who did not know anything about the script or plot) was informed by Stainton what was about to happen so Irwin could prepare and ad-lib as much as he wanted or needed.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d02\", \"start\": 566, \"end\": 574, \"text\": \"Cheyenne\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 41, \"text\": \"the five films in the Ice Age franchise .\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d03\", \"start\": 42, \"end\": 203, \"text\": \"[ 51 ] On Metacritic , the film has a weighted average score of 34 out of 100 based on reviews from 27 critics , indicating `` generally unfavorable reviews '' .\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d03\", \"start\": 204, \"end\": 307, \"text\": \"[ 52 ] Audiences polled by CinemaScore gave the film an average grade of `` B+ '' on an A+ to F scale .\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d03\", \"start\": 308, \"end\": 492, \"text\": \"[ 39 ] Katie Walsh of Los Angeles Times gave the film a negative review , writing that `` Collision Course is simply a perfunctory , watered-down entry in the series that feels like it\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Collision Course\", \"scope\": \"genre\", \"claim\": \"The genre of \\\"Collision Course\\\" is action-comedy.\", \"answer\": \"action-comedy\", \"quote\": \"Collision Course (1989 film) Collision Course is a 1989 action-comedy film starring Jay Leno as a Detroit police officer and Pat Morita as a Japanese officer forced to work together to recover a Japanese turbocharger stolen by a thief played by Chris Sarandon.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0432-c787f6688202:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Collision Course\", \"scope\": \"genre\", \"claim\": \"The genre of \\\"Collision Course\\\" is science fiction.\", \"answer\": \"science fiction\", \"quote\": \"Collision Course (Silverberg novel) Collision Course is a science fiction novel by American author Robert Silverberg, first published in hardcover in 1961 by Avalon Books and reprinted in paperback as an Ace Double later that year.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"action-comedy\", \"science fiction\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"action-comedy\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"science fiction\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
